(2942043, 408107, 30982, '<td valign="top">Sweet portrait, Michele - I quite like this!  The crease in the neck and the very short hair tell me he''s an honest working man - I don''t know exactly why, but that''s what I see.  Tell him thanks for being such a good sport, too.</td>', 'Sweet portrait, Michele - I quite like this!  The crease in the neck and the very short hair tell me he''s an honest working man - I don''t know exactly why, but that''s what I see.  Tell him thanks for being such a good sport, too.', '2006-10-18 22:04:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(2942385, 408010, 64571, '<td valign="top">Great shot, Sandy!  Congrats on the score and your finish!!!</td>', 'Great shot, Sandy!  Congrats on the score and your finish!!!', '2006-10-18 23:25:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(2942423, 406551, 58430, '<td valign="top">this is soooo good!  i love it!  wish I had such creativity</td>', 'this is soooo good!  i love it!  wish I had such creativity', '2006-10-18 23:37:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(2942670, 407816, 61818, '<td valign="top">Very nice shot.  Sorry normally I''m more verbose, but that pretty much sums it up.  Nice shot, pleasant to look at.</td>', 'Very nice shot.  Sorry normally I''m more verbose, but that pretty much sums it up.  Nice shot, pleasant to look at.', '2006-10-19 00:38:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(2942905, 408562, 42013, '<td valign="top">In the context of DPC, i guess i''m suprised this pic scored where it did. I realize flag=low vote for many people but technically the picture is spot on. And even though the idea behind the photo is not clear to me, it''s still quirky and also artistic. It also meets the challenge in an obvious way. <br/> <br/>I remain confused about this one.</td>', 'In the context of DPC, i guess i''m suprised this pic scored where it did. I realize flag=low vote for many people but technically the picture is spot on. And even though the idea behind the photo is not clear to me, it''s still quirky and also artistic. It also meets the challenge in an obvious way.  I remain confused about this one.', '2006-10-19 02:38:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(2942907, 408234, 42013, '<td valign="top">Profound, and something many of us aspire to be.</td>', 'Profound, and something many of us aspire to be.', '2006-10-19 02:39:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(2943131, 408224, 52296, '<td valign="top">Well executed, wonderful colours, congrats to your fourth place Bragi!</td>', 'Well executed, wonderful colours, congrats to your fourth place Bragi!', '2006-10-19 05:21:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2943360, 407884, 28064, '<td valign="top">Well done, great mood<br/></td>', 'Well done, great mood', '2006-10-19 09:16:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(2943563, 408110, 66270, '<td valign="top">I have to say I love the superposition... and the outfit really suits the title... great idea... really love the picture...</td>', 'I have to say I love the superposition... and the outfit really suits the title... great idea... really love the picture...', '2006-10-19 11:25:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(2943647, 407667, 48389, '<td valign="top">Great position in the frame and your use of DOF is really good. I bet it wasn''t easy to expose for this shot with whites on the guys uniform! I think I would have to agree with Rina that because of all the colour in the background even with your shallow DOF it is still a little distracting. Never the less, I think this is a nice image....and at least you let the guy have both his hands this time ;o)</td>', 'Great position in the frame and your use of DOF is really good. I bet it wasn''t easy to expose for this shot with whites on the guys uniform! I think I would have to agree with Rina that because of all the colour in the background even with your shallow DOF it is still a little distracting. Never the less, I think this is a nice image....and at least you let the guy have both his hands this time ;o)', '2006-10-19 11:56:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(2943665, 407233, 48389, '<td valign="top">Well, certainly fits the challenge in my eyes! Great use of DOF here and I am impressed at how well you have controlled your exposure in this shot as there are a lot of different shades of whites (if that makes sense!).</td>', 'Well, certainly fits the challenge in my eyes! Great use of DOF here and I am impressed at how well you have controlled your exposure in this shot as there are a lot of different shades of whites (if that makes sense!).', '2006-10-19 12:02:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(2944145, 407399, 38418, '<td valign="top">This is a great candid shot very cleverly framed</td>', 'This is a great candid shot very cleverly framed', '2006-10-19 14:21:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2944441, 408110, 56015, '<td valign="top">Great photoshop work and very cleverly done.<br/></td>', 'Great photoshop work and very cleverly done.', '2006-10-19 16:17:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(2944626, 408213, 3936, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Review:<br/> <br/>Technical:  Focus and depth of field are excellent.  Color, saturation and hue are excellent as well.  Even the brightest areas are not burned out, yet whites do not look dingy. Skin tones are natural, other colors are not over processed, which is desireable in this photo.<br/> <br/>Reaction:  I like the pose.  The white shirt may be a little clean or out of place for a real cowgirl.  White doesn''t stay white long on a working ranch.  I love the texture of the barn, but at teh same time wonder of the picture might work a bit better if it were softened a bit through a shallower depth of field.  While it is beautiful, it does compete a little bit.  Only other thing is I wish I could see what she is looking at.<br/> <br/>Overall an excellent photo.  Congratulations on your top 20 finish.<br/></td>', 'Critique Club Review: Technical:  Focus and depth of field are excellent.  Color, saturation and hue are excellent as well.  Even the brightest areas are not burned out, yet whites do not look dingy. Skin tones are natural, other colors are not over processed, which is desireable in this photo. Reaction:  I like the pose.  The white shirt may be a little clean or out of place for a real cowgirl.  White doesn''t stay white long on a working ranch.  I love the texture of the barn, but at teh same time wonder of the picture might work a bit better if it were softened a bit through a shallower depth of field.  While it is beautiful, it does compete a little bit.  Only other thing is I wish I could see what she is looking at. Overall an excellent photo.  Congratulations on your top 20 finish.', '2006-10-19 17:22:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2944701, 408257, 66970, '<td valign="top">great hdr</td>', 'great hdr', '2006-10-19 17:54:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(2944729, 408257, 67167, '<td valign="top">Very Nice!</td>', 'Very Nice!', '2006-10-19 18:05:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2945728, 406551, 58728, '<td valign="top">This is stunning.  Perfect.  I LOVE this image. YOu are so talented.  ;)</td>', 'This is stunning.  Perfect.  I LOVE this image. YOu are so talented.  ;)', '2006-10-19 23:40:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(2946123, 407521, 17148, '<td valign="top">:: Critique Club ::<br/> <br/>First off I like the image.  I like the objects in the background are a bit out of focus. I do like your processing to an extent.  Good in B&amp;W and even like the graineven though it was added.  A few things I wish were differentdont like how the hand and head are soft, out of focus. The jacket is the only thing that is sharp. I would like to see a bit more of the waterbut I guess thats not necessary.  I wanted to see that this guy was really sailing on a boatmaybe a shot with the mass, but dont know if that would have been too cluttered. Ultimately I dont know if this was posed or you went to take a photo and he did that. If it was the later then I like it as isspontaneous and candid. If not there might have been a more compelling angle to get more of the boat or wateror both. Like I said I do like the shotdifferent for DPCwhich is very good. <br/> <br/>Clint</td>', ':: Critique Club :: First off I like the image.  I like the objects in the background are a bit out of focus. I do like your processing to an extent.  Good in B&W and even like the graineven though it was added.  A few things I wish were differentdont like how the hand and head are soft, out of focus. The jacket is the only thing that is sharp. I would like to see a bit more of the waterbut I guess thats not necessary.  I wanted to see that this guy was really sailing on a boatmaybe a shot with the mass, but dont know if that would have been too cluttered. Ultimately I dont know if this was posed or you went to take a photo and he did that. If it was the later then I like it as isspontaneous and candid. If not there might have been a more compelling angle to get more of the boat or wateror both. Like I said I do like the shotdifferent for DPCwhich is very good.  Clint', '2006-10-20 01:45:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(2946143, 408181, 17148, '<td valign="top">:: Critique Club ::<br/> <br/>Great job keeping your eyes open for this one. I assume that is a real tattoo and not a stick on. Did he know you were taking thisif so I would have asked him to turn somewhere with a better background. This photo has big potential pretty much as is if the background were more appealing. There is a slight glare on his headbut you might not have had the time nor his patience to ask him to do anything else for this photoand thats if he even knows your shooting him.  As I can see there is nothing to technical about thissure you just snapped it off. The cool thing is the subject and that is well done by you for spotting it. I think you scored fairly well on itman if that bike were totally in the frame you might have broke 6...in my book.</td>', ':: Critique Club :: Great job keeping your eyes open for this one. I assume that is a real tattoo and not a stick on. Did he know you were taking thisif so I would have asked him to turn somewhere with a better background. This photo has big potential pretty much as is if the background were more appealing. There is a slight glare on his headbut you might not have had the time nor his patience to ask him to do anything else for this photoand thats if he even knows your shooting him.  As I can see there is nothing to technical about thissure you just snapped it off. The cool thing is the subject and that is well done by you for spotting it. I think you scored fairly well on itman if that bike were totally in the frame you might have broke 6...in my book.', '2006-10-20 01:53:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(2946159, 408453, 17148, '<td valign="top">:: Critique Club ::<br/> <br/>I like the B&amp;W and those little hands hiding her face. I think a few things that might have hurt just a bit are that the crop is a bit tighta little bit wider would have added more mood to see her whole head and her arms coming upalso the highlights seem a tiny bit blown. If the flash was more soft then it would look that more pleasant. Its not bad just turning the wrong way to being too harsh. Think you did well and placed good for thisI wonder if she did that on her own?</td>', ':: Critique Club :: I like the B&W and those little hands hiding her face. I think a few things that might have hurt just a bit are that the crop is a bit tighta little bit wider would have added more mood to see her whole head and her arms coming upalso the highlights seem a tiny bit blown. If the flash was more soft then it would look that more pleasant. Its not bad just turning the wrong way to being too harsh. Think you did well and placed good for thisI wonder if she did that on her own?', '2006-10-20 01:59:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2946487, 408562, 51538, '<td valign="top">Nice to read the explanation and I would have given a little more than my 5 vote had I spent more time mulling it over.</td>', 'Nice to read the explanation and I would have given a little more than my 5 vote had I spent more time mulling it over.', '2006-10-20 07:44:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(2946573, 408015, 54228, '<td valign="top">had to be you. beautiful work again.</td>', 'had to be you. beautiful work again.', '2006-10-20 09:18:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(2946725, 407397, 65744, '<td valign="top">I think it is a little too dark.  It is kind of hard to make out what everything is.  Try lightening it up a bit next time.</td>', 'I think it is a little too dark.  It is kind of hard to make out what everything is.  Try lightening it up a bit next time.', '2006-10-20 10:48:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(2946770, 408110, 33361, '<td valign="top">I think this image is fabulous!!! <br/> <br/>BUT why is the magazine allowed?? I thought artwork (including magazine covers) were not allowed.. if they are then why aren''t other artistic images allowed (like monitor images)? Just want clarification : )</td>', 'I think this image is fabulous!!!  BUT why is the magazine allowed?? I thought artwork (including magazine covers) were not allowed.. if they are then why aren''t other artistic images allowed (like monitor images)? Just want clarification : )', '2006-10-20 11:02:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2947091, 406551, 57260, '<td valign="top">This is truly creative. Refreshingly different. It''s good to see something other than the super-neatened mega-dodged-and-burned thunderous storm clouds cliché shots win.</td>', 'This is truly creative. Refreshingly different. It''s good to see something other than the super-neatened mega-dodged-and-burned thunderous storm clouds cliché shots win.', '2006-10-20 13:50:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(2947504, 408521, 57775, '<td valign="top">This is a very creative and well done photo.  I love the colors and your position.  My only suggestion would be to run it through Neat Image for the grain.</td>', 'This is a very creative and well done photo.  I love the colors and your position.  My only suggestion would be to run it through Neat Image for the grain.', '2006-10-20 17:02:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2947685, 405140, 55838, '<td valign="top">I think this image should have scored higher.  It''s such a lovely moment that perfectly meets the challenge.  Love the DOF and the softness and the contrasting dark and light.  Very nicely done.</td>', 'I think this image should have scored higher.  It''s such a lovely moment that perfectly meets the challenge.  Love the DOF and the softness and the contrasting dark and light.  Very nicely done.', '2006-10-20 18:38:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2947744, 408425, 3936, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Review:<br/> <br/>Technical:  focus and depth of field are good.  Nice use of a shallow depth of field to reduce background distractions.  Color, saturation and hue are OK.  Lighting is a bit off, the bright highlight on the tree steals the show from the ghost somewhat.<br/> <br/>Reaction:  The straw at lower left distracts some, along witht the very bright highlight on the tree.  The image would have worked better had the ghost been highlighted.  The ghost is a bit centered, but not a fatal problem.  Some people might have voted you down a bit, seeing eyes as part of a face.  I like the backround colors and pattern.  I think the big problem is I like it too much.  The background is great, but it makes the ghost look a little weak in comparison.  It''s just more or less a ghost hanging in a tree in front of a cool background.  If the ghost were better lit, and perhaps a bit larger in the frame, it might work better.<br/></td>', 'Critique Club Review: Technical:  focus and depth of field are good.  Nice use of a shallow depth of field to reduce background distractions.  Color, saturation and hue are OK.  Lighting is a bit off, the bright highlight on the tree steals the show from the ghost somewhat. Reaction:  The straw at lower left distracts some, along witht the very bright highlight on the tree.  The image would have worked better had the ghost been highlighted.  The ghost is a bit centered, but not a fatal problem.  Some people might have voted you down a bit, seeing eyes as part of a face.  I like the backround colors and pattern.  I think the big problem is I like it too much.  The background is great, but it makes the ghost look a little weak in comparison.  It''s just more or less a ghost hanging in a tree in front of a cool background.  If the ghost were better lit, and perhaps a bit larger in the frame, it might work better.', '2006-10-20 19:08:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2948352, 407850, 14476, '<td valign="top">Sheryll,  you asked me to take a look at this image and I am delighted to do so.  I''m going to pretend this is a Critique Club evaluation, so here goes.  "Between a Mother and Son"<br/> <br/>First, I admire your courage in trying new and unusual things.  I very much like the use of complementary colors (purple &amp; yellow).  The image fills the frame nicely and has a lot of interest.<br/> <br/>IMO, I think you have given us a great deal of information in this image and you might consider trying a simpler background if you have another try.  Also, your boy is really quite a bit out of focus and since he is pretty close to being the important foreground, it''s important (I think) that he be sharper.  You should be able to do this, in a nighttime shot, by using a higher ISO rating. And by bracketing your shots.  I understand that is hard to do with a small child, but still, worth a try if you can.  By all means, keep that tripod handy.<br/> <br/>Then, and I do like unorthodox framing, so don''t take this as a suggestion to be more conventional.  I do think you have quite alot of leg and rearend in the foreground, but all the interest is concentrated in the sweetness of the faces and head area.  So, perhaps a bit closer to the area of interest might be worth a try. But not, necessarily, a ''closeup.'' <br/> <br/>Finally, borders and frames are controversial at DPC.  I tend to avoid them and those who use them successfully, tend to be the ones who use the procedure sparingly.  In any case, I''m not sure it enhances this very nice image.<br/> <br/>You have received some very good and perceptive comments on this image from others at DPC.  And I, too, wish you the very best here at DPC and look forward to seeing more of your work.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Sheryll,  you asked me to take a look at this image and I am delighted to do so.  I''m going to pretend this is a Critique Club evaluation, so here goes.  "Between a Mother and Son" First, I admire your courage in trying new and unusual things.  I very much like the use of complementary colors (purple & yellow).  The image fills the frame nicely and has a lot of interest. IMO, I think you have given us a great deal of information in this image and you might consider trying a simpler background if you have another try.  Also, your boy is really quite a bit out of focus and since he is pretty close to being the important foreground, it''s important (I think) that he be sharper.  You should be able to do this, in a nighttime shot, by using a higher ISO rating. And by bracketing your shots.  I understand that is hard to do with a small child, but still, worth a try if you can.  By all means, keep that tripod handy. Then, and I do like unorthodox framing, so don''t take this as a suggestion to be more conventional.  I do think you have quite alot of leg and rearend in the foreground, but all the interest is concentrated in the sweetness of the faces and head area.  So, perhaps a bit closer to the area of interest might be worth a try. But not, necessarily, a ''closeup.''  Finally, borders and frames are controversial at DPC.  I tend to avoid them and those who use them successfully, tend to be the ones who use the procedure sparingly.  In any case, I''m not sure it enhances this very nice image. You have received some very good and perceptive comments on this image from others at DPC.  And I, too, wish you the very best here at DPC and look forward to seeing more of your work. ', '2006-10-21 00:31:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(2948493, 408110, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>First of all, congrats on yet another ribbon, as well as your second highest scoring photo to date.  I''ll also provide a bit of clarification, as least as I understand it, for chispa.  As long as the "artwork" is not the subject of the image, it is allowed.  In this example, it is not the subject, rather it is a small portion of the overall composition.<br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> Everything looks nicely focused and very crisp.  The tonal range is also very nice, thus making this image particularly appealing.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b>  Great, even lighting here with no losses in blown highlights or dark shadows.  The reflection on the top right of the magazine cover is mildly distracting, but not nearly enough to detract from the overall scoring of the image.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> Absolutely wonderful for this challenge.  You hit the challenge on the nose, meanwhile presenting a issue that faces young girls climbing into maturity.  I like it!  The placement of the magazine is spot on, as is the placement of your "props."  Very nice work.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> Personally, I think this one deserved second.  While the first two shots in the challenge are nice, my favorite is 5th place, submitted by jaded_youth, followed very closely by this one.  Another well-deserved ribbon and top score.<br/> <br/>Eric<br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  First of all, congrats on yet another ribbon, as well as your second highest scoring photo to date.  I''ll also provide a bit of clarification, as least as I understand it, for chispa.  As long as the "artwork" is not the subject of the image, it is allowed.  In this example, it is not the subject, rather it is a small portion of the overall composition. Camera Work/Technical: Everything looks nicely focused and very crisp.  The tonal range is also very nice, thus making this image particularly appealing. Lighting:  Great, even lighting here with no losses in blown highlights or dark shadows.  The reflection on the top right of the magazine cover is mildly distracting, but not nearly enough to detract from the overall scoring of the image. Composition/Content: Absolutely wonderful for this challenge.  You hit the challenge on the nose, meanwhile presenting a issue that faces young girls climbing into maturity.  I like it!  The placement of the magazine is spot on, as is the placement of your "props."  Very nice work. My Opinion: Personally, I think this one deserved second.  While the first two shots in the challenge are nice, my favorite is 5th place, submitted by jaded_youth, followed very closely by this one.  Another well-deserved ribbon and top score. Eric', '2006-10-21 03:03:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2948511, 405518, 22537, '<td valign="top">Really an intersting choice of angle and moment.  I think you chose wisely as it illustrates the need to "put your head down and go to work". The emphasis on the shadows eliminates the need to dispaly facial expression yet conveys the story. I think you''ve presented a well thought out portrayal of an entity embarking in one of life''s tasks.  Nice work.</td>', 'Really an intersting choice of angle and moment.  I think you chose wisely as it illustrates the need to "put your head down and go to work". The emphasis on the shadows eliminates the need to dispaly facial expression yet conveys the story. I think you''ve presented a well thought out portrayal of an entity embarking in one of life''s tasks.  Nice work.', '2006-10-21 03:54:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(2948523, 408490, 3936, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Review:<br/> <br/>Technical: Focus and depth of field are excellent.  Color, saturation and hue are very good, with the exception of the skin tones.  Skin tones are a bit blue.  Is he suffocating?<br/> <br/>Reaction:  After reading your comments, it is a wonder he could breathe.  Then again, looking at the skin tones, perhaps he wasn''t. ;-)<br/> <br/>I really like what you''ve done here, but at the same time, the camera angle and lighting makes him look a bit flat.  Had he turned his head a bit, there would have been much more depth to the picture.  Which I feel would have helped some.  <br/> <br/>As is, very creative, and I really like the colors and energy of the piece.  Nice job!<br/></td>', 'Critique Club Review: Technical: Focus and depth of field are excellent.  Color, saturation and hue are very good, with the exception of the skin tones.  Skin tones are a bit blue.  Is he suffocating? Reaction:  After reading your comments, it is a wonder he could breathe.  Then again, looking at the skin tones, perhaps he wasn''t. ;-) I really like what you''ve done here, but at the same time, the camera angle and lighting makes him look a bit flat.  Had he turned his head a bit, there would have been much more depth to the picture.  Which I feel would have helped some.   As is, very creative, and I really like the colors and energy of the piece.  Nice job!', '2006-10-21 04:13:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2948777, 408257, 46870, '<td valign="top">wow wish to go there ,,,,,,,,, cool man       <br/> <br/>congrats on your red!! <br/> <br/> <br/></td>', 'wow wish to go there ,,,,,,,,, cool man        congrats on your red!!   ', '2006-10-21 10:44:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2948949, 408228, 48389, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club Hjalti!</b> <br/> <br/>Firstly, congratulations on your 14th place finish! :o)<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/> <br/>I really like your choice of a more square crop to this shot, the models position in the frame is excellent and you have a good use of negative space above her. I would agree with one of your commenters, I am not sure that the ribbons help this shot, but then other commenters have said they like them. I suppose its personal taste, but to me the ribbons say ''party'' yet the title tells me something different. Maybe I am not really getting the ''essence'' of the person?<br/> <br/><b>Technicals:</b> <br/> <br/>The high key effect works extremely well with the models tones and the minimalist look you have going on in your overall image. I think your lighting is excellent and there is some good detail in the models skin.<br/> <br/>Overall an excellent image and great finish, well done :o)<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>- Natalya :o)<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club Hjalti!  Firstly, congratulations on your 14th place finish! :o) Composition:  I really like your choice of a more square crop to this shot, the models position in the frame is excellent and you have a good use of negative space above her. I would agree with one of your commenters, I am not sure that the ribbons help this shot, but then other commenters have said they like them. I suppose its personal taste, but to me the ribbons say ''party'' yet the title tells me something different. Maybe I am not really getting the ''essence'' of the person? Technicals:  The high key effect works extremely well with the models tones and the minimalist look you have going on in your overall image. I think your lighting is excellent and there is some good detail in the models skin. Overall an excellent image and great finish, well done :o) If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. - Natalya :o)', '2006-10-21 13:11:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(2949097, 406151, 27763, '<td valign="top">Oooh... nice one.  I love the light/tones/mood.  This looks awesome on my monitor, but maybe for people with uncalibrated/dark monitors, it may appear a bit dark.  Oh well, their loss ;)<br/> <br/></td>', 'Oooh... nice one.  I love the light/tones/mood.  This looks awesome on my monitor, but maybe for people with uncalibrated/dark monitors, it may appear a bit dark.  Oh well, their loss ;) ', '2006-10-21 14:37:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(2949112, 406151, 32754, '<td valign="top">This was an incredibly beautifully conceived image...it has great depth and as graphicfunk said, it is gallery worthy.</td>', 'This was an incredibly beautifully conceived image...it has great depth and as graphicfunk said, it is gallery worthy.', '2006-10-21 14:50:37.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(2949171, 406670, 48389, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club Guðbjörg!</b> <br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/> <br/>I like the position of the ''model'' in the frame and your choice of location is intriguing. I would agree with some of your commenters that the cross needs to be more defined, as it is now it blends in with the trees too much and isn''t as noticable as it could be. It also looks to me as if the ''model'' is wearing  pyjamas (bed clothes?) which seems out of place and is confusing me a little. The railings on the very edge of the right handside of the frame are a little distracting too.<br/> <br/><b>Technicals:</b> <br/> <br/>I think B&amp;W suits the subject and adds to the mood of the image. I am no photoshop expert so can not offer serious technical advice all I would suggest is as above, if its possible to use photoshop to bring out the cross a little more from the background this would really help.<br/> <br/><b>My Personal thoughts:</b> <br/> <br/>This image has so much potential, it is already a powerful shot but I feel isolating the ''model'' and cross a little would add even more strength and emotion to the overall image.<br/> <br/>I would love to know your thinking behind this shot and its title if you get time to explain I would really appreciate it :o)<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>- Natalya :o)</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club Guðbjörg!  Composition:  I like the position of the ''model'' in the frame and your choice of location is intriguing. I would agree with some of your commenters that the cross needs to be more defined, as it is now it blends in with the trees too much and isn''t as noticable as it could be. It also looks to me as if the ''model'' is wearing  pyjamas (bed clothes?) which seems out of place and is confusing me a little. The railings on the very edge of the right handside of the frame are a little distracting too. Technicals:  I think B&W suits the subject and adds to the mood of the image. I am no photoshop expert so can not offer serious technical advice all I would suggest is as above, if its possible to use photoshop to bring out the cross a little more from the background this would really help. My Personal thoughts:  This image has so much potential, it is already a powerful shot but I feel isolating the ''model'' and cross a little would add even more strength and emotion to the overall image. I would love to know your thinking behind this shot and its title if you get time to explain I would really appreciate it :o) If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. - Natalya :o)', '2006-10-21 15:35:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(2949610, 408482, 62807, '<td valign="top">I just came across this phtoto and had to say what an absolutly beautiful shot. I like the colors, shows that even through sadness she is  still a little girl full of life. Reminds me of my own little girl and my father who has passed away. I could''t stop looking at it! Adding to my favorites. Great job!!!!!<br/>Debbie</td>', 'I just came across this phtoto and had to say what an absolutly beautiful shot. I like the colors, shows that even through sadness she is  still a little girl full of life. Reminds me of my own little girl and my father who has passed away. I could''t stop looking at it! Adding to my favorites. Great job!!!!!Debbie', '2006-10-21 18:57:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2950097, 404994, 25678, '<td valign="top">Soni!  Good to see you again!  Congratulations on a beautiful fall picture!<br/> <br/>ETA:  I thought the same think Angela did... her left foot is sickled out! It makes the picture quite endearing!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-10-21 21:24:19.</i></td>', 'Soni!  Good to see you again!  Congratulations on a beautiful fall picture! ETA:  I thought the same think Angela did... her left foot is sickled out! It makes the picture quite endearing!', '2006-10-21 22:23:26.000000', '2006-10-21 22:24:19.000000', 0),
